    {
      "text": "Twelve men with this high calling constitute an administrative council in the work of the ministry. When a vacancy occurred with the death of Judas Iscariot, Matthias was divinely appointed to that special office as a member of the council (Acts 1:15–26). Today twelve men with this same divine calling and ordination constitute the Quorum of the Twelve Apostles in The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.",
      "references": [
        {
          "text": "Acts 1:15–26",
          "start": 241,
          "end": 253,
          "parsed": {
            "volume": "nt",
            "bookKey": "acts",
            "book": "acts",
            "chapter": 1,
            "chapterId": "acts1",
            "verses": [
              {
